Relative/seed payoff:
- exists_matrix_opens_supportLocus_subset_twisted_chartInter_of_forall_self
- ThetaGeneratorSeed.exists_matrix_opens_supportLocus_subset_twisted_chartInter

Thus a generator seed's own fibre_regular field gives finite residue support; an explicit GL2 matrix avoids its P1-image; properness spreads confinement to a Zariski neighbourhood. The module and root aggregator build successfully. This closes the infinite-field branch stated in this row. Small finite fields remain the separate finite-Galois/fppf descent obligation selected by widen-decision; the row explicitly warned they cannot be solved by two k-rational avoided points.`;
const certBody=`REJECTED AS FORMULATED after the gated audit.

The requested in-place restatement is type-theoretically wrong. DivRepGlobalData.equiv represents DivFamZar for one fixed map pi, and its theta windows, cocycle, evaluation maps, and DivScheme all depend on that same pi. A witness M changes pi to twistedP1Map pi M, hence changes the fixed representing chart. No single existing DivRepGlobalData.equiv can classify the union over M.

The correct architecture is an OUTER twist-indexed atlas: retain each fixed-(twistedP1Map pi M) DivFamZar and its existing classifier as one chart, then glue/quotient those charts on divisor-equality overlaps. The quantifier over M belongs inside the base-local atlas cover, but outside each fixed classifier. Rewriting IsLocallyCertified/DivFamZar in place would destroy the classifier contract and force the false equivalence this row itself flags.

The two prerequisites did land: p1-aut (af99f2b70) and the full infinite-field fibre-avoidance/seed-spread package (c6a47016f). They support the outer-atlas replacement, not this in-place refactor. Small finite fields additionally require the finite-Galois/fppf descent selected by widen-decision.`;
