      "id": "AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-d.ddr.certificate.widen-decision",
      "title": "DECIDE the widening of DivFamZar: R1 (Aut(P^1) twist) vs R2 (piece type) vs R3 (drop IsLocallyCertified for relative effective Cartier)",
      "projects": [
        "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild"
      ],
      "summary": "THE CAMPAIGN'S ONE LIVE DECISION (opened run 0048 round 5).\n\nWHY IT EXISTS. Inbox I-0365 and informal/w4-rep-critical-path.md section 7.6: the gate is not U2 and not 'a certificate for the universal family'. DivFamZar is BY DEFINITION a quotient of locally certified families (DivisorFamilyZar.lean:224,:235), so certificates are free on the consuming side; the no-go (DivSchemeCertZarC1.lean:123,:131) makes divFunctor a PROPER SUBFUNCTOR of degree-g relative divisors, and a too-small divisor functor cannot cover Pic^0. The obstruction is dat-b B-6 / L8, Zariski-local surjectivity of Sigma.desc f. Every repair below is a WIDENING of DivFamZar, and must be judged by whether L8 becomes true -- not by whether a certificate becomes easier.\n\nSHARPENING WORTH KEEPING: the no-go is VACUOUS FIBREWISE. Over a field the support of a divisor is a finite set of closed points, so IsPreconnected forces a single point, which cannot meet two disjoint fibres. The blindness is purely relative -- a family over a positive-dimensional base whose total support is a connected horizontal curve sweeping from pi^-1(0) to pi^-1(infinity). Base shrinking cannot evade it because every neighbourhood of the crossing meets both sides. So Riemann-Roch-level coverage is untouched; it is presheaf local surjectivity, tested on arbitrary scheme tests, that fails.\n\nTHE THREE CANDIDATES.\n R1  Quantify the certificate over a twist gamma in Aut(P^1_k). Leaves p1-aut -> fibre-avoid ->\n     cert-relocalize. Correct IFF |P^1(k)| >= g+2 (field-size, done). Since Challenge.lean states\n     the Jacobian over an ARBITRARY field and archon-protected.yaml forbids adding a hypothesis\n     (verified: the file's own header says agents are read-only on these signatures), R1 CANNOT\n     discharge the challenge alone; it needs Galois/fppf descent behind it. NOTE the sibling's\n     ZariskiDescentRepresentability.lean is ZARISKI descent and does not cross a field extension;\n     the usable substrate is the sibling's GaloisDescent/ (semilinear algebras and modules,\n     sorry-free, built).\n     STATUS OF ITS FIRST BRICK: Curve/P1Aut.lean landed round 5 and is rooted.\n R2  Generalise FinCoverData's piece type from basic opens of the two pinned charts to arbitrary\n     affine opens of the relative curve. Field-uniform. Justification is one line: supp D is finite\n     over R hence contained in a single affine open (Stacks 0B8B), so a cover with one straddling\n     piece always exists. Blast radius measured round 5: FinCoverData is named in 28 files.\n R3  NEW, and it should be costed beside the other two: drop IsLocallyCertified altogether and use\n     the STANDARD relative effective Cartier divisor (finite locally free of rank g over the base).\n     That object carries no chart-adaptation artifact at all, so the no-go simply does not arise.\n     It is the mathematically standard functor; the cost is re-basing the DivScheme layer on it.\n\nWHAT WOULD DECIDE IT: a costing of R1's descent half against R2's refactor against R3's re-basing,\neach in concrete declarations. Do not start any of the three before this row is closed -- p1-aut\nalready says 'do not attempt both', and R3 makes that a three-way.",
