      "summary": "THE COST OF REPAIR R1 (spec-dd-r ADDENDUM 3 \u00a73). Every declaration in the DD-R chain is generic\nin pi, constrained only by [IsFinite pi] / [IsAffineHom pi] (+ [IsDominant pi]) and\nhpi : pi >> P1.structureMap k = C.left -> Spec k (DivSchemeSeedUnivFields.lean:58). So replacing\npi by gamma . pi for gamma in Aut(P^1_k) costs NOTHING in the landed material: every lemma\napplies verbatim to the twisted map, and the twisted charts pi^-1(P^1 \\ {c}) are affine because\npi is affine.\n\nWHAT IS MISSING: Aut(P^1) does not exist in this project. P1 k is a Proj (Curve/P1.lean:135)\nwith chartOpen : Fin 2 -> Opens (:200); a workspace-wide search finds no PGL_2 action, no Mobius\ntransformation and no automorphism of P1 anywhere.\n\nOBLIGATION. (i) The GL_2(k) action on Proj (k[X_0,X_1]) as a scheme automorphism \u2014 mathlib's\nProj functoriality for graded ring isomorphisms is the intended route; check what this exact\nmathlib rev ships before hand-rolling. (ii) Transitivity on P^1(k), or the weaker form actually\nneeded: for any two distinct c_0, c_1 in P^1(k) an automorphism carrying them to [1:0], [0:1].\n(iii) The compatibility hpi is preserved (gamma is over k), and fiberTwoCover (gamma . pi) is the\ngamma-twisted two-chart cover.\n\nALTERNATIVE IF THIS IS TOO EXPENSIVE: repair R2 (generalize FinCoverData to sigma-charts, the\nnon-vanishing loci of theta sections). Wider refactor, stays inside the relThetaSections\nvocabulary, owes affineness of the complement of an ample divisor. Do not attempt both.\n",
