      ],
      "summary": "THE INTERFACE CHANGE (spec-dd-r ADDENDUM 3 \u00a73, repair R1). Restate IsLocallyCertified \u2014 hence\nDivFamZar and divFunctor \u2014 to quantify over the P^1-coordinate twist as well as over the Zariski\ncover of the base: \"locally on Spec R there is a gamma such that the adaptation is certified for\ngamma . pi\".\n\nWHY THE SHAPE IS FORCED: chart-avoid (c) exhibits a relative divisor that is certified for NO\ngamma-free cover, and confine-open shows the avoidance condition is open on the base, so the\nquantifier must sit inside the base-local one, not outside it.\n\nBLAST RADIUS TO AUDIT (the S6 spelling freeze is a two-lane coordination point, ADDENDUM 1 item\n1 \u2014 the DD-R lane must sign off before S6 freezes): IsLocallyCertified (DivisorFamilyZar.lean),\nDivFamZar / DivFamZar.mk / mapAlg / toZar / exists_glue_of_away_compat / eq_of_away_eq,\ndivFamZar.eval (DivisorFamilyZarVehicle.lean:209), divFunctor\n(DivisorFamilyZarFunctor.lean:45), DivFamZar.exists_certified_away_rep\n(DivRepClassifyZarKit.lean:79), DivFamZar.exists_certChartCover (DivRepClassifyZarKit.lean:433),\nIsLocallyCertified.of_divEq (DivisorFamilyZar.lean:86), and DivRepGlobalData's `equiv` field\n(DivRepKit.lean:83) \u2014 which asserts a full equivalence for a FIXED pi and therefore CANNOT hold\nas stated; it must be re-pinned in the same pass.\n\nGATED ON p1-aut + fibre-avoid. Do not start before both land: the restatement is only worth\nmaking once the twisted charts are known to cover.\n",
